IMPORT prelude

-- Currency Act 1967 (Singapore) -- the Singapore dollar and its use (ss 11, 12), legal tender and its limits (s 13), notes and
-- coins "illegally dealt with" (s 13(6), (7)), private bearer notes (s 14), demonetisation (s 18), mutilated money (s 19),
-- pictures and imitations of money (s 20), defacing money and the IBNS exceptions (s 23), arrest and prosecution (ss 25, 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1967.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amending Act annotated
-- in the body is 6/2019 (with 31/2017 and 15/2010). The deposit's metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0072 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what a person paying, being paid, handling or picturing money meets. Not encoded: Part 2 (the 2002
-- transfer from the Board of Commissioners of Currency to the Authority, ss 3-10), the exchange arrangements and fees (s 15, which
-- depend on prescribed conditions not deposited), form and design (s 17), the dissolved Currency Fund and the asset backing
-- (ss 21, 22), seizure of counterfeits (s 24), the certificate of genuineness (s 13(8), (9)), regulations (s 28) and the savings
-- (s 29). The Penal Code offences on counterfeiting, which s 23(4) preserves, are not in this Act and not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Currency Act 1967 -- tender`

§§ `11, 12 -- the Singapore dollar`

-- s 11(1): "The unit of currency of Singapore is the Singapore dollar, which is divided into 100 cents." (2) "S$" or "SGD".
-- s 12: "All monetary obligations or transactions in Singapore are deemed to be expressed and recorded, and must be settled in the
-- Singapore dollar unless otherwise provided for by law or validly agreed upon between the parties."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cents in a Singapore dollar` MEANS 100

GIVEN `another law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `the parties validly agreed another currency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obligation must be settled in Singapore dollars` IF
    (NOT `another law provides otherwise`) AND (NOT `the parties validly agreed another currency`)

§§ `13 -- legal tender`

-- s 13(1): only notes and coins issued by the Authority are legal tender. (2): notes "if the notes have not been illegally dealt
-- with, are legal tender up to their face value for the payment of any amount". (3): coins likewise, but only "for the payment of
-- an amount not exceeding 20 times the face value of a coin of that denomination". (4): where "a payee has given written notice to
-- the payer that the payee would not accept as payment all or any of the denominations", (2) or (3) does not apply to the extent
-- specified. (5): where no such notice was given, payment under (2) or (3) "is deemed to have satisfied that debt".
-- s 13(6)(a): a coin is illegally dealt with where "impaired, diminished, or lightened otherwise than by fair wear and tear", or
-- defaced "by having any name, word, device or number stamped or engraved" on it. (b): a note where "impaired, diminished or
-- affected otherwise than by fair wear and tear", or defaced "by writing or impressing on any note any mark, word, letter or figure
-- or by perforation, cutting, splitting or in any other manner". (7): a note is also illegally dealt with if "mutilated, destroyed
-- or permanently damaged ... as a result of the activation of an IBNS".
-- s 18(1): a withdrawn issue or denomination "upon such withdrawal cease[s] to be legal tender".
-- The limit in (3) is on the AMOUNT OF THE PAYMENT, read literally, not on the coins' share of it. Amounts are in cents.
DECLARE Tender HAS
    `is a coin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `face value in cents` IS A NUMBER
    `payment due in cents` IS A NUMBER
    `issued by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `withdrawn by Gazette notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `impaired otherwise than by fair wear and tear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defaced by a mark, writing or cutting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged by an IBNS activation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payee gave written notice refusing the denomination` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it has been illegally dealt with` IF
        `the tender`'s `impaired otherwise than by fair wear and tear`
    OR  `the tender`'s `defaced by a mark, writing or cutting`
    OR  ((NOT `the tender`'s `is a coin`) AND `the tender`'s `damaged by an IBNS activation`)

GIVEN `face value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest payment coins of this face value can make` MEANS
    `face value` TIMES 20

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is legal tender for the payment` IF
        `the tender`'s `issued by the Authority`
    AND (NOT `the tender`'s `withdrawn by Gazette notification`)
    AND (NOT `it has been illegally dealt with` `the tender`)
    AND (NOT `the tender`'s `payee gave written notice refusing the denomination`)
    AND (    (NOT `the tender`'s `is a coin`)
         OR  `the tender`'s `payment due in cents` AT MOST `the largest payment coins of this face value can make` (`the tender`'s `face value in cents`))

§§ `14 -- private bearer notes`

-- s 14(1): no person, "except with the permission of the Authority", may (a) "draw, accept, make or issue any bill of exchange,
-- promissory note or engagement for the payment of money payable to bearer on demand"; or (b) borrow on such bills or notes.
-- (2): "Cheques or drafts payable to bearer on demand may be drawn on bankers or agents by their customers" against moneys held.
-- (3): liable on conviction by a Magistrate's Court "to a fine equal to the amount of the bill, note or engagement ... even if the
-- amount of such fine may be in excess of the original jurisdiction of such Court".
GIVEN `issued a bearer-on-demand note` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Authority's permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a cheque on a banker against funds held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `issuing it contravenes section 14` IF
    `issued a bearer-on-demand note` AND (NOT `had the Authority's permission`) AND (NOT `it is a cheque on a banker against funds held`)

GIVEN `amount of the note` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 14 fine` MEANS `amount of the note`

§§ `18 -- demonetisation`

-- s 18(2): a withdrawal notification "must give holders ... a reasonable period, in any event at least 6 months, within which such
-- notes or coins may be exchanged at their face value". (Whether a period of 6 months or more is "reasonable" is not decided here.)
GIVEN `months allowed for exchange` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exchange period meets the 6-month floor` IF
    `months allowed for exchange` AT LEAST 6

§§ `19 -- mutilated notes and coins`

-- s 19(1): "A person is not entitled to recover from the Authority the value of any mutilated currency note or coin or any note or
-- coin which has been illegally dealt with." (2): a refund "as an act of grace" is "in the absolute discretion of the Authority".
-- (3): such notes and coins "must be repossessed" when tendered to the Authority.
GIVEN `is mutilated` IS A BOOLEAN, `is illegally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 19 bars recovery of its value` IF
    `is mutilated` OR `is illegally dealt with`

GIVEN `is mutilated` IS A BOOLEAN, `is illegally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority must repossess it when tendered` IF
    `is mutilated` OR `is illegally dealt with`

§§ `20 -- pictures and imitations of money`

-- s 20(1): "Except with the permission of the Authority", a person must not (a) "in any size, scale or colour, use any photograph
-- of or any drawing or design resembling any currency note or coin or part thereof, in any advertisement"; or (b) import,
-- manufacture, sell, circulate or distribute merchandise containing one. (2): nor merchandise "containing any design or part thereof
-- used in or on any currency note or coin". (4): a person must not make or issue a piece of any material "resembling or similar to
-- any coin" -- with NO permission exception. (5): fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 months or both.
-- A photograph outside an advertisement and not on merchandise (for example in a news article) is outside (1) and (2) as written.
DECLARE MoneyImage IS ONE OF
    `a photograph of a note in an advertisement`
    `a drawing resembling a coin in an advertisement`
    `merchandise printed with a picture of a note`
    `merchandise using a design element from a note`
    `a token resembling a coin`
    `a photograph of a note in a news article`

GIVEN `the use` IS A MoneyImage, `had permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 20` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `a token resembling a coin` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a photograph of a note in a news article` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `had permission`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 20 maximum fine` MEANS 2000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 20 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 3

§§ `23 -- mutilating, destroying or defacing money`

-- s 23(1): an offence for any person who (a) "mutilates or destroys any currency note or coin"; (b) "causes any change in a coin so
-- as to destroy or diminish its value or utility"; (c) "prints or stamps, or by any similar means writes, or impresses, on any
-- currency note any mark, word, letter or figure"; or (d) "defaces any coin by stamping thereon any name or word". Fine not
-- exceeding $2,000 (no imprisonment).
-- (2): a licensed security service provider who sells an IBNS or uses one in cash-in-transit services is not, "by reason only of
-- such sale or employment", liable under (1)(a) for mutilating or destroying a NOTE or (1)(c), where caused by the activation of
-- the IBNS. (3): the same for an applicant for such a licence, for activation "in any trial or demonstration of the applicant's
-- IBNS that is required by a licensing officer". (4): the section does not limit the Penal Code 1871.
DECLARE MoneyAct IS ONE OF
    `mutilating or destroying a note`
    `mutilating or destroying a coin`
    `changing a coin to diminish its value`
    `printing or stamping a mark on a note`
    `stamping a name or word on a coin`
    `spending a worn note`

GIVEN `the act` IS A MoneyAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is within section 23(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `spending a worn note` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the act` IS A MoneyAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the IBNS exceptions can reach the act` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `mutilating or destroying a note` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `printing or stamping a mark on a note` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the act` IS A MoneyAct, `caused by IBNS activation` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed to sell or use the IBNS` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a trial required by a licensing officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an offence under section 23` IF
        `the act is within section 23(1)` `the act`
    AND NOT (    `the IBNS exceptions can reach the act` `the act`
             AND `caused by IBNS activation`
             AND (`licensed to sell or use the IBNS` OR `in a trial required by a licensing officer`))

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 23 maximum fine` MEANS 2000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 23 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 0

§§ `25, 26 -- arrest and prosecution`

-- s 25: any police officer "may arrest without warrant" a person offending in view against, or reasonably suspected of
-- contravening, "section 14, 20 or 23". s 26: "No prosecution for any offence under this Act may be instituted without the consent
-- of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under the section is arrestable without warrant` IF
    `section number` EQUALS 14 OR `section number` EQUALS 20 OR `section number` EQUALS 23

GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented`
